#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059566 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "7bfcfcbb-6212-5f9b-90aa-c79fbf7221e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4518" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](images/21/212a3beac5ede3786bad835a693b0a725f331de41d6969dce7f17925dde012d7.svg)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/22/22034036ec7859b56e9e19124e33fa616eddfc3784e15f8074583e28253a4bae.svg)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/b5/b5e0f47e7c4bb15e8923bceb665dcc87944090e3a39f9a335b17ab0b85025cc8.svg)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/b6/b643463daef16c2179d6f6320d31353a23b042f3774295eb55e48af0242ec655.svg)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/bf/bf8fb79fd8998c5c867fc371535e26f2e92bea5fa7262789bd44aea07e24f93c.svg)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "c4af8b0d-e4ee-56f4-9cf6-594530639339" :question/math-academy-id "e-4519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](images/22/228e4520f4301ac7acb7eef54fad6dcc8ce9bbf43d48124a761978dfcea6423b.svg)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/80/80100c3398fa2eac3a07696dd30354c3c971f0650ab32d67a958492ed1cbdeae.svg)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/8f/8f7fdfc0426ad23a34e6d7f2915181a88a63ea74da93b2b6bd718e03f21ba8d2.svg)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/28/2867d40f70d0e042e522e1bb14ea8af830e42f22a63cc482ba67923c51807312.svg)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/9a/9a4c39673ffd559b35ed9dbf0e465f6a8714c0d9a467178a51e1f6ad79a81445.svg)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01601b6f-c05d-574c-9a4a-d776d7830de4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426727} {:answer/id #uuid "4d9e88a0-7c5e-5e8c-9e9a-14296af074a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-1,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426732} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f35897-b61a-57d6-81d6-9ea4cf4754e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=1,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426735} {:answer/id #uuid "df865a24-76e9-5e0c-aef0-ccb73198892d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426739} {:answer/id #uuid "f375eeb9-cae0-5b47-8162-0ab390a8e5ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=3,\\,c=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01601b6f-c05d-574c-9a4a-d776d7830de4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426727} :answer-field/id #uuid "456a058b-2a76-50e4-b196-28caf276666d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426748}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06d7e42a-14b7-5ba4-9656-a3c1d06d273b" :question/math-academy-id "q-10006" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z=0 \\\\ x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & b \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ a & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y-z=0 \\\\ x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61b6213e-6630-5cbc-a2be-bba26537e9d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263842} {:answer/id #uuid "98683e89-44c4-5b63-a6a0-5143070e1a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=8,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264311} {:answer/id #uuid "a16f2ca2-4f2e-5acc-9b55-06d4bbfa6420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=8,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264374} {:answer/id #uuid "dc08dfd2-1ae1-53cb-adad-40873d7ac878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264916} {:answer/id #uuid "f9db3e03-47ba-53e0-8851-1e7f8c0aa7b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9db3e03-47ba-53e0-8851-1e7f8c0aa7b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265185} :answer-field/id #uuid "21ecd5d5-730f-53a8-b7fd-5892a28e6ac7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "718180b1-bf73-575f-add7-0f6c8d9bba0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130536" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ -6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85806f6e-3f8d-56f5-8841-0e3c0a47083a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #u