db/ref 17592186298185} :answer-field/id #uuid "cda9e946-5a85-5e86-9781-1b1870f198bf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "193f944c-d77c-5446-9a05-12850a3f60de" :question/math-academy-id "q-316961" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-1$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :questi